    "bodyHtml": "<p>ATEEZ closes their most successful album series yet this week: <strong>GOLDEN HOUR : Part.6 arrives Friday, November 13, 2026</strong> — the 15th mini album, the final chapter of the GOLDEN HOUR saga, and it's arriving with <strong>\"UP\"</strong> as its title track. The series that produced three Billboard 200 No. 1s is ending on ATEEZ's terms, and ATINY has been counting down since the first teaser dropped. Here's everything confirmed so far.</p>\n\n<h2>Key details</h2>\n\n<table>\n  <tr><th><strong>Detail</strong></th><th><strong>Info</strong></th></tr>\n  <tr><td>Album</td><td>GOLDEN HOUR : Part.6 (15th mini album)</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Release date</td><td>November 13, 2026</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Tracks</td><td>5 (tracklist revealed October 25)</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Title track</td><td>\"UP\"</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Pre-release</td><td>\"Drip\" (October 23)</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Series status</td><td>Final chapter — closes the GOLDEN HOUR series</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Announced</td><td>October 7–8 with the \"CRASH TO BEGIN\" spoiler video</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h2>The GOLDEN HOUR series — the whole run at a glance</h2>\n\n<p>To understand why Part.6 carries heavyweight expectations, look at what the series has already done:</p>\n\n<table>\n  <tr><th><strong>Chapter</strong></th><th><strong>Released</strong></th><th><strong>Milestone</strong></th></tr>\n  <tr><td>GOLDEN HOUR : Part.1</td><td>2024</td><td>Series opener</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>GOLDEN HOUR : Part.2</td><td>November 2024</td><td>ATEEZ's second Billboard 200 No. 1</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>GOLDEN HOUR : Part.3</td><td>Mid-2025</td><td>Kept the cadence — roughly one part every 4–5 months</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>GOLDEN HOUR : Part.4</td><td>February 6, 2026</td><td>\"Adrenaline\" era</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>GOLDEN HOUR : Part.5</td><td>2026</td><td>ATEEZ's <strong>third Billboard 200 No. 1</strong></td></tr>\n  <tr><td>GOLDEN HOUR : Part.6</td><td><strong>November 13, 2026</strong></td><td>Series finale — title track \"UP\"</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>Three Billboard 200 No. 1 albums inside one series. That's the streak \"UP\" is walking into — and why first-week numbers for Part.6 will be watched across the industry, not just by ATINY.</p>\n\n<h2>How the comeback was rolled out — day by day</h2>\n\n<p>KQ Entertainment announced the album on October 7–8 with a cryptic <strong>\"CRASH TO BEGIN\"</strong> spoiler video — and confirmed the line fans had been bracing for: Part.6 <strong>ends the GOLDEN HOUR series</strong>. The rollout since has been a masterclass in pacing:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>October 23:</strong> pre-release single <strong>\"Drip\"</strong> dropped — and landed on the <strong>Billboard Global 200 in its first chart week</strong>, with Korean press describing the group's chart rise as \"scary\" (their word, not ours).</li>\n  <li><strong>October 25:</strong> the <strong>5-track tracklist</strong> was revealed, confirming \"UP\" as title track, plus the first MV teaser.</li>\n  <li><strong>November 5:</strong> a full album preview landed on YouTube — the \"Part.6 Preview\" — alongside news of <strong>one-night-only release parties</strong>.</li>\n  <li><strong>November 10:</strong> a new \"UP\" MV teaser dropped, teasing an expanded-universe concept for the video.</li>\n  <li><strong>November 13:</strong> album + \"UP\" MV at release. The series closes.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>\"Drip\" — the statement the album walks in on</h2>\n\n<p>Pre-release singles set the temperature, and \"Drip\" set it high: a groovy, sleek MV, immediate fan traction, and a <strong>Billboard Global 200 debut in week one</strong> — before the album even had a tracklist. The Korea Herald flagged ATEEZ's chart milestone with \"Drip\" in early November, and the Sports Chosun \"rise getting scary\" framing captured the consensus: ATEEZ's global numbers have stopped being a surprise and started being a pattern.</p>\n\n<h2>Where to celebrate release week</h2>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>November 13:</strong> album + \"UP\" MV at release — the one-night-only release parties follow the drop</li>\n  <li><strong>November 20–22:</strong> HMV UK hosts in-store celebrations for UK ATINY</li>\n  <li><strong>Streaming now:</strong> the Part.6 album preview on ATEEZ's official YouTube if you want the full sound before Friday</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>How to pre-order Part.6 (for the latecomers)</h2>\n\n<p>Pre-orders have been open since early October through standard channels:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Weverse Albums / official KQ store</strong> — the platform-native option, usually with platform benefits</li>\n  <li><strong>Korean music retailers</strong> — the standard first-week chart-count route</li>\n  <li><strong>Western retailers</strong> — for Billboard-charting physical sales, US/international retailers ship worldwide</li>\n  <li><strong>Collect-the-series note:</strong> as the GOLDEN HOUR finale, Part.6 completes the six-part physical set — expect demand from completionist ATINY on top of first-week buyers</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>One honest note: the five track titles beyond \"UP\" and \"Drip\" haven't all been highlighted in the coverage we reviewed — check the official tracklist poster for the full five-song picture rather than fan-compiled guesses.</p>\n\n<h2>What \"the end of GOLDEN HOUR\" means</h2>\n\n<p>Series finales in K-pop are rare on this scale — most multi-part runs fizzle or pivot. ATEEZ closing GOLDEN HOUR after three Billboard No. 1s, a Billboard Global 200 pre-release, and a global tour cycle means the group is ending its hottest streak on a deliberate high note. Whatever comes after Part.6 starts from a taller summit than the series did.</p>\n\n<h2>FAQ</h2>\n\n<h3>When does ATEEZ GOLDEN HOUR Part.6 come out?</h3>\n<p>Friday, November 13, 2026 — worldwide release.</p>\n\n<h3>What's the title track?</h3>\n<p>\"UP,\" one of five tracks on the mini album, with its music video premiering at release. A second MV teaser dropped November 10 teasing an expanded-universe concept.</p>\n\n<h3>What was the pre-release single?</h3>\n<p>\"Drip,\" released October 23 — it entered the Billboard Global 200 in its first chart week.</p>\n\n<h3>Is Part.6 the end of the GOLDEN HOUR series?</h3>\n<p>Yes — KQ confirmed this final chapter closes the series that produced ATEEZ's three Billboard 200 No. 1 albums.</p>\n\n<h3>How many Billboard No. 1s does ATEEZ have?</h3>\n<p>Three — Part.2 (November 2024), and two more across the 2025–2026 chapters, with Part.5 delivering the third in 2026.</p>\n\n<h3>Are there release events?</h3>\n<p>One-night-only release parties were announced for release week, and HMV UK runs in-store celebrations November 20–22.</p>\n\n<h3>What's after GOLDEN HOUR?</h3>\n<p>Nothing announced yet as of November 10, 2026 — KQ has kept the focus on Part.6's finale. Whatever's next, ATINY will hear it first through official channels.</p>\n\n<p><em>Sourced from KQ Entertainment announcements, Billboard, Korea Herald, allkpop, Soompi and Nolae. Accurate as of November 10, 2026.</em></p>",
