    "bodyHtml": "<p>TOMORROW X TOGETHER's most intense era yet lands Monday: <strong>PERFECT STORM, the group's 9th mini album, releases November 16, 2026</strong> — six tracks \"capturing the turbulence of youth,\" led by title track <strong>\"Angel Bite.\"</strong> The pre-campaign numbers are already the biggest of TXT's career: a No. 1 Spotify global pre-save chart debut, pre-orders surging to 3.5× their previous album, and a world tour notice dropped before the album even arrived. Here's the full comeback briefing as of November 10, 2026.</p>\n\n<h2>Key details</h2>\n\n<table>\n  <tr><th><strong>Detail</strong></th><th><strong>Info</strong></th></tr>\n  <tr><td>Album</td><td>PERFECT STORM (9th mini album)</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Release date</td><td>November 16, 2026</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Tracks</td><td>6 (tracklist + motion film revealed October 30)</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Title track</td><td>\"Angel Bite\" — MV with the album</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Theme</td><td>The turbulence of youth / growing pains</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Pre-save ranking</td><td>No. 1 on Spotify's global pre-save chart (October 27)</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Pre-order surge</td><td>3.5× the group's previous album</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h2>The rollout — day by day</h2>\n\n<p>BIGHIT MUSIC opened the era in late September with an <strong>interactive comeback website</strong> and a promise of \"something different from anything before\" — and then kept every single week loaded:</p>\n\n<table>\n  <tr><th><strong>Date</strong></th><th><strong>What dropped</strong></th></tr>\n  <tr><td>Late September</td><td>Comeback announced; interactive website live — \"different from anything before\"</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>October 11–12</td><td>Pre-save/pre-order surge reported at 3.5× the last album</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>October 20</td><td>Dramatic album trailer + full comeback schedule</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>October 20–22</td><td>Concept rollout framed around Gen Z \"youth pain\"</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>October 26</td><td>Weverse notice: a <strong>TOMORROW X TOGETHER WORLD TOUR</strong> is coming</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>October 27</td><td>No. 1 on Spotify's global pre-save chart</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>October 29</td><td>\"PERFECT STORM : THE MOVIE\" Weverse event announced</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>October 30</td><td>Tracklist + motion film — six songs, \"Angel Bite\" confirmed as title</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>November 4–5</td><td>All-track preview clips; Mnet M2 comeback showcase confirmed; 100M-won showcase pledge story</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>November 10</td><td>Yongsan pop-up store opens — inspired by the \"Angel Bite\" MV</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>November 16</td><td>Album + \"Angel Bite\" MV release</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h2>The \"Angel Bite\" era — why it matters</h2>\n\n<p>\"Angel Bite\" is being positioned as the album's emotional core — a \"youth-pain\" title track in line with the concept film's turbulence-of-youth framing. The idea running through the whole rollout: <strong>growing up hurts, and this album doesn't pretend otherwise.</strong> Korean coverage has framed it as TXT's rawest direction yet — which tracks with the group's catalog arc from the bright dream-pop of their early era through progressively heavier youth-focused concepts.</p>\n\n<p>And the confidence flex that told you everything: TXT <strong>pledged a 100 million won penalty if the Mnet M2 showcase recording wasn't attended properly</strong> — a guarantee-of-effort joke that doubled as a statement of stakes. When a group bets that kind of money on their own performance, expectations aren't subtle.</p>\n\n<h2>The physical and digital fan experience</h2>\n\n<p>This era is unusually loaded with real-world touchpoints:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Yongsan pop-up store</strong> — opened November 10, inspired by the \"Angel Bite\" MV; photo ops and exclusive merch</li>\n  <li><strong>\"PERFECT STORM : THE MOVIE\"</strong> — a special Weverse event announced October 29</li>\n  <li><strong>Mnet M2 comeback showcase</strong> — the performance showcase landing with release</li>\n  <li><strong>WITHMUU fan-signing events</strong> — running through the promo cycle</li>\n  <li><strong>Interactive comeback website</strong> — live since late September, still the era's puzzle-box hub</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>And then: a world tour</h2>\n\n<p>The October 26 Weverse notice confirmed what the album title hinted at — a <strong>TOMORROW X TOGETHER world tour</strong> is being teed up around this era. Dates and details are rolling out through official channels; if you're MOA, the move is to keep notifications on. Tours that launch off a fresh album mean the \"Angel Bite\" stage will be built for arenas from day one.</p>\n\n<h2>Why the pre-campaign numbers matter</h2>\n\n<p>A 3.5× pre-order surge and a Spotify global pre-save No. 1 before release aren't just nice graphs — they're the leading indicators the industry reads for first-week trajectory. Combined with a six-track album (shorter albums concentrate streams and sales) and a title track with a built-in concept hook, PERFECT STORM is positioned for a monster first week. Chart-watchers will be looking at Billboard 200 debuts and domestic first-day numbers the morning of November 17.</p>\n\n<h2>FAQ</h2>\n\n<h3>When does TXT PERFECT STORM come out?</h3>\n<p>Monday, November 16, 2026.</p>\n\n<h3>What's the title track?</h3>\n<p>\"Angel Bite,\" with its music video premiering alongside the album — the \"youth-pain\" centerpiece of a six-track album.</p>\n\n<h3>How many songs are on PERFECT STORM?</h3>\n<p>Six tracks, revealed via tracklist poster and motion film on October 30.</p>\n\n<h3>Why is this comeback called \"different from anything before\"?</h3>\n<p>The concept framing is the turbulence of youth — a rawer, storm-themed direction teased from the first trailer and the interactive comeback website, and reflected in the \"Angel Bite\" MV aesthetics.</p>\n\n<h3>Is TXT going on tour?</h3>\n<p>A world tour notice was posted on Weverse on October 26 — dates and details are rolling out through official channels.</p>\n\n<h3>What is the 100 million won pledge about?</h3>\n<p>TXT pledged a 100 million won penalty if their Mnet M2 comeback showcase recording wasn't properly attended — a headline-grabbing confidence flex that doubled as a performance guarantee, and a story Korean media ran throughout promo week.</p>\n\n<p><em>Sourced from BIGHIT MUSIC, Weverse, Korea Times, Korea Herald, Chosunbiz, allkpop and Soompi. Accurate as of November 10, 2026.</em></p>",
