    "bodyHtml": "<p>Ten years after \"Chewing Gum,\" NCT DREAM just released their most meaningful album yet: <strong>DREAM AFTER DREAM, the 6th full-length album, dropped November 9, 2026</strong> — the centerpiece of the group's 10th-anniversary year, led by disco-funk title track <strong>\"Boogie Woogie.\"</strong> It's also the first full album of a new six-member era, it's topping charts on day one, and it arrives with a new leader at the helm. Here's the complete picture as of November 10, 2026.</p>\n\n<h2>Key details</h2>\n\n<table>\n  <tr><th><strong>Detail</strong></th><th><strong>Info</strong></th></tr>\n  <tr><td>Album</td><td>DREAM AFTER DREAM (6th full-length album)</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Release date</td><td>November 9, 2026</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Title track</td><td>\"Boogie Woogie\" — disco funk, MV out now</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Pre-release</td><td>\"The Sun\" (October 20)</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Members</td><td>Six — first album since Mark's departure</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>New leader</td><td>Jeno (confirmed November 10)</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>Chart status</td><td>Topping album and digital charts (day one)</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h2>The 10-year journey — how DREAM got here</h2>\n\n<p>Few K-pop groups hit a 10th anniversary with their original youth identity intact. NCT DREAM debuted in August 2016 as the teenage unit of NCT — and a decade later, here's how the anniversary year has actually unfolded:</p>\n\n<table>\n  <tr><th><strong>Date</strong></th><th><strong>Milestone</strong></th></tr>\n  <tr><td>June 15</td><td>10th-anniversary project announced on Weverse; hotel-themed fan meeting \"THE SWEET DREAM HOTEL\" revealed — the first after Mark's departure, the first official six-member chapter</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>June 24–25</td><td>Fan meeting sells out <strong>every seat during pre-sale</strong> — the six-member era's demand proven immediately</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>August 7</td><td>\"OUR SUMMER DREAM : NCT DREAM 10\" Weverse notice — the anniversary summer begins</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>August 22</td><td>\"THE SWEET DREAM HOTEL\" kicks off at an Incheon arena</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>August 31</td><td>Seoul glows <strong>champagne green</strong> — the city lights up for NCT's 10th</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>October 15</td><td>\"DREAM AFTER DREAM\" anniversary project officially announced</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>October 16</td><td>6th full album confirmed for November 9</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>October 20</td><td>Pre-release single <strong>\"The Sun\"</strong> — a reflective look back at a decade together</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>October 22</td><td>Official comeback schedule poster</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>October 28–29</td><td>Title track reveal: <strong>\"Boogie Woogie\"</strong> — disco funk, lyrics contributed by <strong>Jaemin</strong></td></tr>\n  <tr><td>November 3</td><td><strong>Seongsu pop-up</strong> opens for the album</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>November 5</td><td>Choreography news: <strong>LEEJUNG</strong> reunites with NCT DREAM for \"Boogie Woogie\"</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>November 9</td><td>Album + MV at midnight — the members tell Korean press: <em>\"the past 10 years have felt like a dream\"</em></td></tr>\n  <tr><td>November 10</td><td>Album tops album and digital charts; <strong>Jeno confirmed as new leader</strong></td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h2>A new six-member era — the honest context</h2>\n\n<p>This is the anniversary album's bigger frame: <strong>Mark departed NCT DREAM in 2026</strong>, and DREAM AFTER DREAM is the group's first full album as six. The transition was handled the fandom-first way — announced around the fan-meeting cycle, tested live at Incheon in August where the sold-out pre-sale answered any demand questions, and now sealed with an album that topped charts on day one.</p>\n\n<p>And the leadership question that defined the era's opening weeks got its answer: <strong>Jeno steps in as the group's new leader</strong> as of November 10 — the six-member era now has its structure, its sound, and its sold-out receipts.</p>\n\n<h2>Why \"Boogie Woogie\" is the right title track</h2>\n\n<p>After ten years, the members chose a party over a requiem — and the details make it special:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Jaemin wrote lyrics.</strong> A member's pen on the anniversary single turns the celebration personal — the group narrating its own decade.</li>\n  <li><strong>LEEJUNG choreographed it.</strong> The choreographer behind some of the group's most beloved moments reunited with NCT DREAM for the anniversary dance — announced November 5, five days of anticipation before the MV.</li>\n  <li><strong>Disco funk over balladry.</strong> NCT DREAM's story has always been youth — and the 10-year mark is being marked with joy rather than nostalgia alone. \"The Sun\" handles the reflective half; \"Boogie Woogie\" throws the party.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>The numbers on day one</h2>\n\n<p>Per Korean chart coverage on November 10, DREAM AFTER DREAM is <strong>topping both album and physical/digital charts</strong> as the comeback lands — the strongest possible opening for an anniversary album, and a clear statement that the six-member era starts with full force. The Seongsu pop-up is running for the album, and the champagne-green Seoul lighting campaign earlier in the year already set the celebratory stage citywide.</p>\n\n<h2>The members' own words</h2>\n\n<p>In the pre-release Q&A with 매일경제 (November 9), the members framed the decade simply: <em>\"The past 10 years have felt like a dream.\"</em> DREAM AFTER DREAM — the title isn't abstract; it's the group's own summary of where ten years landed, and what comes after the dream: the second decade, six members, one new leader, and a disco party to open it.</p>\n\n<h2>FAQ</h2>\n\n<h3>When did NCT DREAM release DREAM AFTER DREAM?</h3>\n<p>November 9, 2026 — timed as the centerpiece of their 10th-anniversary celebration.</p>\n\n<h3>What's the title track?</h3>\n<p>\"Boogie Woogie,\" a disco-funk track with lyrics contributed by Jaemin and choreography by LEEJUNG. Pre-release single \"The Sun\" came out October 20.</p>\n\n<h3>Is NCT DREAM six members now?</h3>\n<p>Yes — this is the group's first full album since Mark's departure, with Jeno confirmed as the new leader as of November 10.</p>\n\n<h3>How did the album perform at release?</h3>\n<p>It topped album and digital charts on day one, per Korean chart coverage on November 10.</p>\n\n<h3>What was the 10th-anniversary fan meeting?</h3>\n<p>\"THE SWEET DREAM HOTEL\" — a hotel-themed fan meeting that sold out every seat during pre-sale and kicked off August 22, 2026, at an Incheon arena.</p>\n\n<h3>Why is the choreography news a big deal?</h3>\n<p>LEEJUNG — one of K-pop's most in-demand choreographers — reunited with NCT DREAM for \"Boogie Woogie,\" after previously collaborating with the group on fan-favorite stages.</p>\n\n<h3>What does the album title mean?</h3>\n<p>The members answered it themselves: ten years that \"felt like a dream\" — DREAM AFTER DREAM is what comes next.</p>\n\n<p><em>Sourced from SM Entertainment, Weverse, 매일경제, Korea Times, allkpop, Soompi, JoongAng and Bandwagon. Accurate as of November 10, 2026.</em></p>",
